# requirements-dev.txt tells you to run `python3 -m venv .venv` in this
# directory to get a test runner, but nothing ignored it — so anyone who
# followed the documented workflow and then ran `git add -A` would stage a
# whole virtualenv. Same shape as the apps/hub-app/node_modules symlink trap
# (see the hub-chat research notes): the instructions create an artifact the
# ignore rules did not cover.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
